    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can offer personalized tutoring, explain concepts in simple language, and generate practice problems tailored to student levels. They can adapt to learning pace and style, especially helpful for students who struggle with abstract ideas. In schools, they could support teachers and provide instant feedback, making math more accessible and less intimidating."
